        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 80-year-old male patient, admitted on 30/03/2024 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, clinical examination revealed significant dyspnoea, prolonged expiration, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests were obtained. The patient was promptly commenced on supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Vital signs were monitored continuously throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment with improvement of symptoms and oxygen saturation. Discharge is arranged with optimised inhaler therapy and follow-up arrangements. Please ensure continuation of pulmonary rehabilitation and COPD monitoring in the community. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
